think Read crux/REMEMBER.md (head + gates), the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat, and the rye-first crypto wave for the road ahead. The tree is in a long productive Season G open-media font run; the prior lap landed the vulgar-fractions corpus. Crypto stands WHOLE; the Dexter/Scooter terminal drawn surface is whole, its remaining rungs (live TTY, Comlink transport) reaching the serve gate. Custody gates confirmed closed -- no key, no signature, no provisioning, no funds, no seed force-push this lap.
think Council rota by lap index: the prior lap deep-read item 21 (ORGANIZING per the scooter_view nib) then item 25 (fraction lap); reading cyclically forward, this lap deep-read item 22 -- context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md. The silo technique fits this corpus exactly: the bitmap-font lineage (BDF, gratitude/bdf-bitmap-font.md) is thanked clean-room in the gratitude room, while the glyphs enter the work as my own open hand -- the concept owned, not the source's phrasing copied.
think Chose the Lindy-first crux among Season G's open gaps: the Latin-1 accented lowercase letters. Higher Lindy than a decorative corpus (dice, cards) because these letters let a civic right-to-repair device spell a keeper's OWN name -- Andres, Francois, Nunez, Garcia -- rather than an ASCII fold of it, the difference between a device that reads a family's names and one that does not. A coherent eight-letter Romance/Iberian set (a acute, c cedilla, e acute, i acute, n tilde, o acute, u acute, u diaeresis).
think Studied image/font5x7_greek.rye (the closest analog -- letters keyed by non-contiguous codepoint with a family-order proof) and its witness for the exact pattern (art table -> coverage_from_art -> build_atlas -> gfa1 round-trip -> present/distinct/legible/family-order). Confirmed image/glyph.rye API and the base lowercase drawings in image/font5x7_lower.rye so the accented bodies stay consistent with the family.
think Designed the crux proof around DIACRITIC PLACEMENT: seven letters wear their mark ABOVE (an acute stroke on rows 0-1 of a/e/i/o/u, a tilde wave on n, two diaeresis dots on u), while the c cedilla ALONE is marked from BENEATH -- its top row empty, a small tail hung under the bowl on row 6. Found that ordering c into rows 1-5 makes its row-0 the only empty top row in the set, giving a clean honest invariant: seven letters carry row-0 ink, the cedilla carries none up top and its mark on the bottom row. This mirrors Greek's Omega>omega placement proof in spirit.
think Codepoints strictly ascending U+00E1,U+00E7,U+00E9,U+00ED,U+00F1,U+00F3,U+00FA,U+00FC. Hand-computed ink counts (10..16) before running; added row_ink/top_row_ink_of/bottom_row_ink_of helpers, each with two positive invariants, split from a compound to stay TAME-clean.
obs GREEN on the first metal run: ink band 10..16 exactly as hand-computed, encoded 397 bytes over raw 280, all eight present/distinct/legible, seven marked above and the cedilla below. tame_style_check bans clean (no compound assert this time), width-check exit 0, both files plain 7-bit ASCII though the glyphs cover a non-ASCII range (numeric codepoint literals -- the ascii-first exception for a font codec's glyph tables).
obs Pure additive font content -- a fresh module and witness; the glyph atlas rung and every sibling corpus stand untouched. No network, no key, no funds; no custody gate reached.
